{{ ref: 964d1c6a-2dcb-48ae-beb8-4a7f1195507d }}
## 🧭 Guiding Philosophy
--{ ref: 964d1c6a-2dcb-48ae-beb8-4a7f1195507d }--

{{ ref: 172df5e4-1c17-4f14-830c-9bf8ccf44f96 }}
Our architecture is built on a few foundational beliefs:
--{ ref: 172df5e4-1c17-4f14-830c-9bf8ccf44f96 }--

{{ ref: 91efff8f-8698-40dc-9a04-e4d3a3f2160b }}
1. **Operations are atomic and idempotent** — They either fully succeed or fully fail, and repeating them is always safe.
--{ ref: 91efff8f-8698-40dc-9a04-e4d3a3f2160b }--
{{ ref: c3edea8c-749f-4a5a-91a6-858f310ec477 }}
1. **Fail fast, fail clearly** — Validate early, surface errors immediately, never proceed with bad data.
--{ ref: c3edea8c-749f-4a5a-91a6-858f310ec477 }--
{{ ref: a02bbf5c-a5dd-47b9-abe7-7a253fc79859 }}
1. **Immutability over mutation** — Deploy new resources rather than patching existing ones.
--{ ref: a02bbf5c-a5dd-47b9-abe7-7a253fc79859 }--
{{ ref: fa5c17b5-eee6-4876-90ac-96151bcbef07 }}
1. **Defense in depth** — Layer security controls; never rely on a single mechanism.
--{ ref: fa5c17b5-eee6-4876-90ac-96151bcbef07 }--
{{ ref: 91798f9e-1c5e-4d46-a9b2-97e0973193fa }}
1. **Observability by default** — Every service emits logs, metrics, and traces from day one.
--{ ref: 91798f9e-1c5e-4d46-a9b2-97e0973193fa }--

{{ ref: e601ca73-2e5d-45a2-bf3f-af84bfda77ff }}
These principles aren't just guidelines — they're the foundation that makes our codebase predictable and our debugging tractable.
--{ ref: e601ca73-2e5d-45a2-bf3f-af84bfda77ff }--

