{{ ref: 58e90629-bcb4-44a9-81b1-cac4ab9a7e34 }}
## 🔧 Operations Architecture
--{ ref: 58e90629-bcb4-44a9-81b1-cac4ab9a7e34 }--

{{ ref: ed2b7178-b127-47d8-b7f7-5918323bb1b9 }}
Our backend follows an **operation-first architecture**. Business logic lives in service operations, which coordinate data orchestrators for all database access. This separation keeps concerns clean and makes each layer independently testable.
--{ ref: ed2b7178-b127-47d8-b7f7-5918323bb1b9 }--

{{ ref: 37f9c615-a4c8-4d9d-9bc8-396c9298a5de }}
### Service Operations
--{ ref: 37f9c615-a4c8-4d9d-9bc8-396c9298a5de }--

{{ ref: f7a3f610-7c43-4c38-a2ef-29c3c1bb6c5f }}
Service operations contain business logic and are executed by the runtime layer. They:
--{ ref: f7a3f610-7c43-4c38-a2ef-29c3c1bb6c5f }--

{{ ref: c2af6fb7-9349-4962-bdc1-928d95acbf9e }}
- Define typed input/output schemas via manifests
--{ ref: c2af6fb7-9349-4962-bdc1-928d95acbf9e }--
{{ ref: f466569d-5842-4e43-ba81-c998b6e3e104 }}
- Call peer services through typed service agents
--{ ref: f466569d-5842-4e43-ba81-c998b6e3e104 }--
{{ ref: 583ca982-fc16-4e32-8fe4-0d20bd20a3a4 }}
- Access databases **exclusively** through data orchestrators
--{ ref: 583ca982-fc16-4e32-8fe4-0d20bd20a3a4 }--
{{ ref: 8bb62202-308d-451e-9865-fd082e32bfc8 }}
- Integrate with external services (Sentry, Supabase Auth, Stripe, etc.)
--{ ref: 8bb62202-308d-451e-9865-fd082e32bfc8 }--

{{ ref: 6788929b-fa93-4dc5-aabc-aa9c435033b4 }}
### Data Operations
--{ ref: 6788929b-fa93-4dc5-aabc-aa9c435033b4 }--

{{ ref: b3cfc8f5-3f9f-4a47-ba1a-0a016b2dcf75 }}
Data operations are procedures that read from or write to a persistent store. Every data operation must touch a database — that's what defines them.
--{ ref: b3cfc8f5-3f9f-4a47-ba1a-0a016b2dcf75 }--

{{ ref: e74d24cc-e417-460a-974b-17156c292fb2 }}
Each operation is a standalone, **ACID-compliant** unit of work:
--{ ref: e74d24cc-e417-460a-974b-17156c292fb2 }--

{{ ref: 78a2be9b-25fc-453e-a462-5c3faf7b18dd, table_width: 2 }}
| Property   | Guarantee                                                        |
| ---------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Atomic** | Fully succeeds or fully fails — no partial writes                |
| **Consistent** | Schema constraints and business rules are enforced before commit |
| **Isolated** | Concurrent operations don't see intermediate state               |
| **Durable** | Once returned, data is persisted                                 |
--{ ref: 78a2be9b-25fc-453e-a462-5c3faf7b18dd }--

{{ ref: ce0d7a24-93f5-4f9e-80ee-19e02eec650c }}
### Design Implications
--{ ref: ce0d7a24-93f5-4f9e-80ee-19e02eec650c }--

{{ ref: a3607b12-9d0c-4f4c-93f4-028d65dd83c0 }}
These ACID guarantees shape how we design operations:
--{ ref: a3607b12-9d0c-4f4c-93f4-028d65dd83c0 }--

{{ ref: a4c7b7ff-cc4d-45d2-be33-139303a07c60 }}
- **Keep operations small and focused** — one logical change per operation
--{ ref: a4c7b7ff-cc4d-45d2-be33-139303a07c60 }--
{{ ref: 7cea0c63-9e8a-4acc-a8a1-403c57d12ad9 }}
- **Operations are safe to retry** on transient failures
--{ ref: 7cea0c63-9e8a-4acc-a8a1-403c57d12ad9 }--
{{ ref: a1f33beb-c97c-442b-b679-bf736dec9ba1 }}
- **Services compose operations** rather than expanding transaction scope
--{ ref: a1f33beb-c97c-442b-b679-bf736dec9ba1 }--
{{ ref: 4f115e88-98f3-4c4c-a637-6691629cf41d }}
- **Each operation is independently testable** with predictable outcomes
--{ ref: 4f115e88-98f3-4c4c-a637-6691629cf41d }--

{{ ref: 863daea5-3c52-44c9-a7f6-5769c5fe2d4f }}
### Layer Boundaries
--{ ref: 863daea5-3c52-44c9-a7f6-5769c5fe2d4f }--

{{ ref: 501a5f3b-3936-489e-a058-9b19d7018406 }}
Understanding where code belongs keeps each layer focused and testable:
--{ ref: 501a5f3b-3936-489e-a058-9b19d7018406 }--

{{ ref: e7ee90f1-ad7a-46a0-bc62-27f139c63e8d, table_width: 3 }}
| Code Type                       | Where It Belongs         | Principle                                 |
| ------------------------------- | ------------------------ | ----------------------------------------- |
| Database read/write             | Data Operation           | ACID guarantees, single source of truth   |
| Call external API               | Service Operation        | Retry logic, error handling, auth context |
| Orchestrate multiple operations | Service Operation        | Coordinates at business level             |
| Generate embeddings / AI calls  | Service Operation        | External dependency, retriable            |
| Service input/output schema     | Manifest                 | Contract lives with API definition        |
| Validation schema               | Co-located with consumer | Cache adapter owns its cache schema       |
| Parse or transform data         | Shared Library           | Pure function, no side effects            |
| Format output response          | Shared Library           | Deterministic, easily testable            |
--{ ref: e7ee90f1-ad7a-46a0-bc62-27f139c63e8d }--

{{ ref: 13c2f683-1fe2-48d2-96a9-444475e86cbb }}
**Decision guide:**
--{ ref: 13c2f683-1fe2-48d2-96a9-444475e86cbb }--

{{ ref: 40234679-9b29-4cb6-8445-876f42b13d9d }}
- **Touches database?** → Data Operation
--{ ref: 40234679-9b29-4cb6-8445-876f42b13d9d }--
{{ ref: a8e326ee-0a6d-42ec-b6a9-de607457cd9f }}
- **Touches external service?** → Service Operation
--{ ref: a8e326ee-0a6d-42ec-b6a9-de607457cd9f }--
{{ ref: 3bf0b443-853e-46f5-8f7e-959b4f307f6e }}
- **Defines API contract?** → Manifest
--{ ref: 3bf0b443-853e-46f5-8f7e-959b4f307f6e }--
{{ ref: 47a4b8f8-2f58-4b4d-ab7c-c535cccf2f7d }}
- **Validates domain-specific data?** → Co-locate with consumer
--{ ref: 47a4b8f8-2f58-4b4d-ab7c-c535cccf2f7d }--
{{ ref: d0ef69d8-a74a-42d2-846e-2027e3c76438 }}
- **Pure utility with no side effects?** → Shared Library
--{ ref: d0ef69d8-a74a-42d2-846e-2027e3c76438 }--

{{ type: callout, ref: f0cfed32-09b7-4f60-92b9-c62bdb1df48d, color: yellow_background, icon: ⚠️ }}
**Anti-pattern (cross-domain):** Don't create "mega-operations" that touch multiple unrelated domains. Cross-domain coordination belongs at the service layer, with compensation logic — never inside a single data operation or a single `transact` block.
--{ ref: f0cfed32-09b7-4f60-92b9-c62bdb1df48d }--

{{ type: callout, ref: 93fd4acf-a28a-48b5-94d1-bb1f1b777a18, color: blue_background, icon: 🔗 }}
**Intra-domain transactional composition** — when multiple operations *within the same domain* must commit or roll back together, compose them via the orchestrator's `transact` primitive:
  ```typescript
  await <orchestrator>.transact(async (tx) => {
    const entity = await tx.set<Entity>({ /* ... */ });
    await tx.attach<Related>({ entityId: entity.id, /* ... */ });
  });
  ```
  `tx` exposes the same operations as the orchestrator, minus `transact` itself. Each `tx.*` call shares one interactive transaction — atomic commit or rollback. Defaults: `timeout: 3000ms`, `maxWait: 2000ms` (override via `createOrchestrator` options). Use only for single-domain composition; coordinate cross-domain flows at the service layer with compensation logic.
  See [@theriety/prisma]{{ mention: page:66b95120-1519-4778-a1b6-a41e6d85a804 }} for the underlying mechanism and [Different Kinds of Logics]{{ mention: page:379cf3c8-7d3f-49e9-8075-3ce8bcc925f1 }} for where this fits in the data-layer story.
--{ ref: 93fd4acf-a28a-48b5-94d1-bb1f1b777a18 }--

{{ ref: e4063eb7-1951-44b8-bbb9-5ad81bf271e3 }}
### Invocation Paths
--{ ref: e4063eb7-1951-44b8-bbb9-5ad81bf271e3 }--

{{ ref: 7facb78b-719b-43e4-822a-b6691a162346 }}
Operations can be invoked via two distinct paths — **external** (through the API gateway) or **internal** (through the service mesh). The gateway is reserved for client-facing requests; service-to-service calls bypass it entirely.
--{ ref: 7facb78b-719b-43e4-822a-b6691a162346 }--

{{ ref: 1a76fd6c-3187-4c13-9c59-deed3d1ebe21 }}
```mermaid
graph LR
    subgraph "External Path (client → gateway → service)"
        Client["External Client"] -->|"POST /services/{svc}/operations/{op}<br/>Authorization: Bearer external-token<br/>Body: raw payload"| GW["API Gateway"]
        GW -->|"Verify token<br/>Issue initiator JWT<br/>Wrap body as { payload }"| EP["@theriety/endpoint"]
        EP -->|"Feature gating<br/>Dispatch via service agent"| SVC1["Target Service"]
    end

    subgraph "Internal Path (service → dispatcher → service)"
        SVC2["Calling Service"] -->|"action.service.peer.operation(input)<br/>Dispatcher resolves inline or external"| DISP["Dispatcher"]
        DISP -->|"Full OperationRequest envelope<br/>{ payload, cache?, callback?, error? }<br/>+ initiator JWT"| SVC3["Peer Service"]
    end

    style GW fill:#e1f5ff
    style EP fill:#fff4e6
    style DISP fill:#e8f5e9
```
--{ ref: 1a76fd6c-3187-4c13-9c59-deed3d1ebe21 }--

{{ ref: 66934cd3-6884-4e4b-8fc8-827a466df5b8 }}
**Key difference:** The gateway accepts a **raw JSON payload** from external clients and maps it to `{ payload }` only — the `cache`, `error`, and `callback` fields on `OperationRequest` do not exist on the external path. These fields are injected exclusively by the runtime's service agent and async callback machinery during internal dispatch.
--{ ref: 66934cd3-6884-4e4b-8fc8-827a466df5b8 }--

{{ ref: 74330696-4e19-4180-a40d-88750ccda25d, table_width: 3 }}
|                   | **External (Gateway)**           | **Internal (Dispatcher)**                                   |
| ----------------- | -------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Entry point**   | HTTP URL path                    | `action.service.<peer>.<operation>(input)`                  |
| **Auth**          | External Bearer token (OIDC)     | Initiator JWT (internally signed)                           |
| **Body → **`**payload**` | ✅ Raw HTTP body becomes `payload` | ✅ Operation input becomes `payload`                         |
| `**cache**`       | ❌ Not present                    | Injected by runtime for cross-invocation result persistence |
| `**error**`       | ❌ Not present                    | Injected by runtime alongside `cache`                       |
| `**callback**`    | ❌ Not present                    | Injected by service agent for async continuations           |
| `**deferUntil**`  | ❌ Not available                  | Available on `DispatchParams` for scheduled execution       |
| **Feature gating** | ✅ Checked at endpoint layer      | ❌ Bypassed (trusted boundary)                               |
| **Scope enforcement** | ✅ At target service via `ensure()` | ✅ At target service via `ensure()`                          |
--{ ref: 74330696-4e19-4180-a40d-88750ccda25d }--

{{ ref: 7ab51364-10e2-482a-b481-764183bcc2e8 }}
For the full type definitions and developer guide, see the **Request Format** section in [Enforcing Permission]{{ mention: page:d7aa7b9b-641b-4133-995e-357237eb8928 }}.
--{ ref: 7ab51364-10e2-482a-b481-764183bcc2e8 }--

