{{ ref: 4d61ec52-381f-4a2f-8005-5c64d5c8058e }}
## 🏗️ Infrastructure & Deployment
--{ ref: 4d61ec52-381f-4a2f-8005-5c64d5c8058e }--

{{ ref: e409fc40-1f91-4af7-8250-115d449173eb }}
### Immutable Deployments
--{ ref: e409fc40-1f91-4af7-8250-115d449173eb }--

{{ ref: f696fd08-be65-4ba4-a47b-1196d3f5692b }}
Infrastructure changes create new resources rather than mutating existing ones. This makes rollbacks trivial and eliminates configuration drift.
--{ ref: f696fd08-be65-4ba4-a47b-1196d3f5692b }--

{{ ref: dff4b5b5-253d-4941-86fc-05f36b163d4b, table_width: 2 }}
| Action        | Approach                           |
| ------------- | ---------------------------------- |
| Deploy        | Create new Lambda version          |
| Rollback      | Redeploy previous version          |
| Update config | New deployment with updated values |
--{ ref: dff4b5b5-253d-4941-86fc-05f36b163d4b }--

{{ ref: 8ac0ab76-e4d3-49ac-9edb-d5d2450c7559 }}
### Configuration as Code
--{ ref: 8ac0ab76-e4d3-49ac-9edb-d5d2450c7559 }--

{{ ref: 1e2972f2-9246-4552-97f6-bf712e3642e9 }}
All configuration is version-controlled and reproducible. Nothing is configured manually in the console.
--{ ref: 1e2972f2-9246-4552-97f6-bf712e3642e9 }--

{{ ref: 92898612-1b9a-4e44-b6d3-ed4d836ebba0, table_width: 3 }}
| Type           | Storage             | Tool             |
| -------------- | ------------------- | ---------------- |
| Infrastructure | Git repository      | Pulumi           |
| Runtime config | SSM Parameter Store | AWS SDK          |
| Secrets        | Secrets Manager     | Rotation enabled |
--{ ref: 92898612-1b9a-4e44-b6d3-ed4d836ebba0 }--

{{ ref: bfab34c9-8267-4a26-8e6f-ad0b52dfda17 }}
---
--{ ref: bfab34c9-8267-4a26-8e6f-ad0b52dfda17 }--

{{ ref: 88b4e009-77cb-40c4-8a99-4c0e17f4fb67 }}
## 🛡️ Reliability & Resilience
--{ ref: 88b4e009-77cb-40c4-8a99-4c0e17f4fb67 }--

{{ ref: bc995af8-9af0-4539-8e71-b60fdce9fd3d }}
### Idempotency
--{ ref: bc995af8-9af0-4539-8e71-b60fdce9fd3d }--

{{ ref: 4eb20942-a1c9-43bd-aa51-9df2ee07f4a1 }}
The same request executed multiple times produces the same result without side effects. This is essential for safe retries.
--{ ref: 4eb20942-a1c9-43bd-aa51-9df2ee07f4a1 }--

{{ ref: 0a21e33f-633a-4bc6-a1c0-6f2db821783d }}
```typescript
// ✅ idempotent with key
async function createPayment(idempotencyKey: string, amount: number) {
  const existing = await db.findPayment(idempotencyKey);
  if (existing) return existing; // return cached result
  
  return await db.createPayment({ idempotencyKey, amount });
}
```
--{ ref: 0a21e33f-633a-4bc6-a1c0-6f2db821783d }--

{{ ref: 34ac3465-c629-41cf-bd14-fb9ce779a5bf }}
### Retry with Backoff
--{ ref: 34ac3465-c629-41cf-bd14-fb9ce779a5bf }--

{{ ref: c5fe1911-c37d-4592-8d36-970ccc083d5d }}
Transient failures are retried with exponential backoff and jitter. This prevents thundering herds while giving failures time to recover.
--{ ref: c5fe1911-c37d-4592-8d36-970ccc083d5d }--

{{ ref: f0f7dce2-4342-49f2-a73c-e28abfe37954 }}
```typescript
const retryConfig = {
  maxRetries: 3,
  baseDelay: 100,      // ms
  maxDelay: 5000,      // ms
  backoffFactor: 2,
  jitter: true,
};
```
--{ ref: f0f7dce2-4342-49f2-a73c-e28abfe37954 }--

{{ ref: a8b07bfe-bc47-4764-9023-c3ed04134136 }}
### Graceful Degradation
--{ ref: a8b07bfe-bc47-4764-9023-c3ed04134136 }--

{{ ref: 8d86ed48-a66c-464c-9794-4f786cd3c650 }}
Services continue operating with reduced functionality when dependencies fail. A payment service outage shouldn't take down the entire application.
--{ ref: 8d86ed48-a66c-464c-9794-4f786cd3c650 }--

{{ ref: 7af7e165-ae6d-4806-970c-5f6f24862853 }}
### Circuit Breaking
--{ ref: 7af7e165-ae6d-4806-970c-5f6f24862853 }--

{{ ref: 73819af8-d118-46e6-a51d-3e3ea56d76e7 }}
We stop requests to failing dependencies after threshold breaches, preventing cascade failures from overwhelming the system.
--{ ref: 73819af8-d118-46e6-a51d-3e3ea56d76e7 }--

{{ ref: ee3b9847-e74d-4d90-a2da-fcca14345844 }}
---
--{ ref: ee3b9847-e74d-4d90-a2da-fcca14345844 }--

{{ ref: db8f1f14-9e5c-4e98-8613-8ee60b785366 }}
## 🔐 Security
--{ ref: db8f1f14-9e5c-4e98-8613-8ee60b785366 }--

{{ ref: 7ca9dc1b-d2cc-41ff-a99a-5421d12cb350 }}
### Least Privilege
--{ ref: 7ca9dc1b-d2cc-41ff-a99a-5421d12cb350 }--

{{ ref: 886bd528-f6c0-4daa-9c9a-cdd685976920 }}
Services have minimal permissions required for their function. Lambda functions don't get admin access just because it's convenient.
--{ ref: 886bd528-f6c0-4daa-9c9a-cdd685976920 }--

{{ ref: 6f200860-2702-4d7e-b998-61f65c09344c }}
### Defense in Depth
--{ ref: 6f200860-2702-4d7e-b998-61f65c09344c }--

{{ ref: f312cada-538b-41ef-84eb-c600f5c226d6 }}
Security controls are layered. We don't rely on a single mechanism to protect sensitive data or operations.
--{ ref: f312cada-538b-41ef-84eb-c600f5c226d6 }--

{{ ref: f8302763-507e-4224-b7de-940aa41ec5bb, table_width: 2 }}
| Layer          | Control              |
| -------------- | -------------------- |
| Network        | VPC, Security Groups |
| Transport      | TLS 1.3              |
| Authentication | JWT, OIDC            |
| Authorization  | RBAC, Scopes         |
--{ ref: f8302763-507e-4224-b7de-940aa41ec5bb }--

{{ ref: 054a4162-0b6f-4008-aea8-4e87daa4c309 }}
### Secrets Management
--{ ref: 054a4162-0b6f-4008-aea8-4e87daa4c309 }--

{{ ref: 0a6d5ca3-96ed-454f-8e7f-5e9f1789ca70 }}
Secrets are externalized, rotated, and **never committed** to source control. Period.
--{ ref: 0a6d5ca3-96ed-454f-8e7f-5e9f1789ca70 }--

{{ ref: 4b7c7aa4-c853-4231-b780-b329300825b5 }}
---
--{ ref: 4b7c7aa4-c853-4231-b780-b329300825b5 }--

{{ ref: d3b71b82-63b3-4ced-bad5-350c495e9ad9 }}
## 📡 Observability
--{ ref: d3b71b82-63b3-4ced-bad5-350c495e9ad9 }--

{{ ref: 4299f1c2-75c3-49a8-9f18-5ee3871ea6a9 }}
Every service emits logs, metrics, and traces by default. Observability isn't an afterthought — it's built into the runtime.
--{ ref: 4299f1c2-75c3-49a8-9f18-5ee3871ea6a9 }--

{{ ref: 62617973-2ddf-4b8e-a679-25d454f7602f, table_width: 3 }}
| Signal  | Tool       | Purpose                     |
| ------- | ---------- | --------------------------- |
| Logs    | CloudWatch | Debugging, audit trail      |
| Metrics | CloudWatch | Performance, alerting       |
| Errors  | Sentry     | Exception tracking, context |
| Traces  | Sentry     | Distributed request flow    |
--{ ref: 62617973-2ddf-4b8e-a679-25d454f7602f }--

{{ ref: 40259faa-5e43-42c8-8c07-0bdc68864d36 }}
### Distributed Tracing
--{ ref: 40259faa-5e43-42c8-8c07-0bdc68864d36 }--

{{ ref: 0bdab655-d240-4ec8-86f8-8c3e98ce48da }}
Tracing helps us analyze distributed system performance — particularly for identifying bottlenecks and calculating latency costs for each component.
--{ ref: 0bdab655-d240-4ec8-86f8-8c3e98ce48da }--

{{ ref: 76874d4f-f3bc-43ed-aa7a-5685937d56ea }}
A **trace** consists of **spans**, each representing a unit of work done by a component. Spans can be nested, so a span representing a longer-running task can contain multiple spans for the smaller tasks within it.
--{ ref: 76874d4f-f3bc-43ed-aa7a-5685937d56ea }--

{{ ref: 20faa5e5-fd4b-4bc6-844a-dc247870fee0 }}
We use **Sentry** as our distributed tracing system. While it lacks features like service graphs compared to dedicated solutions (Zipkin, Jaeger, Appdash), its rich context for individual events and its position as our exception management tool make it the right choice for us.
--{ ref: 20faa5e5-fd4b-4bc6-844a-dc247870fee0 }--

